  <title>Resource management</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Resources</gui><gui>Resource management</gui></guiseq> keeps
  short entries: a phone call to return, a note about a customer, a job to do.
  Each has a <gui>Subject</gui>, a <gui>Contact</gui>, a <gui>Dated for</gui>
  date, tags, and notes of any length. Changes are saved as you make
  them.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Click <gui>New entry</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click its <gui>Subject</gui> to type it, and its
    <gui>Contact</gui> to choose one. Click <gui>Dated for</gui> to choose a
    date, or <gui>No date</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click its <gui>Tag</gui> to give it a category; see <link
    xref="resource_categories"/>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Double click the entry and type notes in the box beside the
    list.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check <gui>To Do</gui> to put it on the main window's to-do
    list, in its tag's colour.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>When it is dealt with, select it and click <gui>Post entry</gui>. It
  leaves the to-do list and the time clock.</p>

  <section id="list">
  <title>Finding entries</title>
  <p>Narrow the list by <gui>With tag</gui> and <gui>Older than</gui>, choose
  how to <gui>Sort by</gui>, and set the <gui>Row limit</gui>. The up and down
  buttons move the selected entry to sort the list by hand; <gui>Remove manual
  sort</gui> in the window menu undoes that.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="more">
  <title>More</title>
  <list>
    <item><p><gui>Time clock project</gui> makes the selected entry a project
    in the <link xref="time_clock"/>, so time spent on it can be punched; check
    <gui>Open time clock</gui> to open it as well.</p></item>
    <item><p>Right click an entry for its <gui>Contact hub</gui>, to
    <gui>Delete</gui> it, or to <gui>Block number</gui>, which adds its phone
    number to the list of blocked callers.</p></item>
    <item><p>The window menu has <gui>Tags</gui>, to apply several tags to
    the selected entry, and <gui>Report hub</gui>; see <link
    xref="report_hub"/>.</p></item>
  </list>
  </section>

</page>
